12. Transaction Mempool

12.1 Pool Implementation

Thread-safe transaction pool using DashMap for concurrent access:

· Configurable Capacity: Default 10,000 pending transactions.
· Per-Address Limit: Default 100 transactions per address (prevents single-address flooding).
· Nonce Tracking: Per-address pending nonce set for gap detection.
· Priority Index: BTreeMap-based fee-per-byte index for efficient block selection.
· Replacement Policy: Higher-fee transaction replaces same-nonce transaction with +10% fee bump requirement.

12.2 Transaction Validator

Pre-pool validation checks performed before accepting any transaction:

1. Basic Validation: Non-zero addresses, non-zero amount, valid timestamp within acceptable range.
2. Signature Verification: Dispatches by signature length (64 bytes → Ed25519, ~4,595 bytes → Dilithium5).
3. Balance Check: Sufficient balance for amount + fee.
4. Nonce Check: Within acceptable range of current account nonce.
5. Fee Check: Meets minimum fee-per-byte threshold.
6. Dormancy Check: Account has not been dormant for 6+ years.

12.3 Fee Calculator

Market-based fee estimation with congestion awareness:

Component Value
Base Fee 1,000 units (0.001 PNX) per transaction
Minimum Fee 100 units (0.0001 PNX) absolute floor
Fee Per Byte 1 unit (0.000001 PNX)
Congestion Multiplier Activates above 50% mempool capacity, up to 3× at full capacity
Priority Tiers Low, Normal, High, Urgent with corresponding multipliers

12.4 Transaction Ordering

Priority-based transaction selection for block inclusion:

· Score Calculation: Weighted combination of fee-per-byte (70%), age (20%), and size efficiency (10%).
· Nonce Resolution: Dependent transactions ordered by sequential nonce within same address.
· Priority Queue: BinaryHeap-based implementation for efficient max-priority extraction.

12.5 Pool Pruning

Automatic cleanup mechanisms maintain pool health:

· Age-Based: Transactions older than configurable TTL (default 1 hour) are removed.
· Capacity-Based: Lowest-fee transactions removed when pool exceeds max size.
· Per-Address Limit: Oldest transactions removed when per-address limit exceeded.
· Background Pruner: Periodic cleanup task with configurable interval.

