13. Economic Model: Tri-Phase Deflation

The Pacyte economy transitions through three mathematically deterministic phases, each designed to optimize for a different stage of network maturity.

13.1 Phase Evolution

Phase Supply Range Burn Rate (of fees) Validator Share Genesis Vault Share Duration
1. Great Burn 550M → 400M 60% → 90% (increasing linearly) ~36% → 10% (decreasing) ~4% → 0% (decreasing) Until supply reaches 400M
2. Transition 400M → 250M 90% → 0% (decreasing linearly) 10% → 90% (increasing) 0% → 10% (increasing) Until supply reaches 250M
3. Golden Era 250M (Fixed, Permanent) 0% 90% 10% Indefinite

Great Burn Rationale: Early-stage aggressive deflation rewards early adopters by rapidly contracting supply. The burn rate increases linearly from 60% to 90% as supply decreases, creating an accelerating scarcity effect.

Transition Rationale: As supply approaches the target, burn gradually decreases while validator incentives increase to ensure network security remains adequately compensated as the primary deflationary mechanism phases out.

Golden Era Rationale: The permanent supply cap of 250M PNX combined with 0% burn creates a predictable, sustainable economic model where validators earn 90% of transaction fees and the Sovereign Vault receives 10% for ecosystem development.

13.2 Fee Structure

Pacyte uses 6-decimal precision (1 PNX = 1,000,000 base units):

Fee Component Base Units PNX Equivalent Description
Base Fee (per transaction) 1,000 0.001 PNX Minimum fee for any valid transaction
Absolute Minimum Fee 100 0.0001 PNX Absolute floor, applied when base fee would be lower
Fee Per Byte 1 0.000001 PNX Additional fee per byte of transaction data

A standard transfer of approximately 250 bytes incurs the base fee of 0.001 PNX. The fee-per-byte component ensures that larger transactions (smart contract deployments, complex DeFi interactions) pay proportionally higher fees.

13.3 The 6-Year Dormancy Rule

In fixed-supply assets, lost private keys permanently remove coins from circulation. An estimated 20–25% of Bitcoin's supply is believed to be permanently lost.

Solution: Wallets that have not initiated an outgoing transaction for 6 consecutive years (approximately 189 million blocks at 1-second block time) are flagged as dormant. After a successful community governance vote, these funds may be burned or reallocated to the Sovereign Vault for ecosystem development.

Governance Protection: The Dormancy Rule requires a successful community governance proposal to execute. No automatic burning occurs without explicit community consensus, preventing abuse while enabling the protocol to maintain a healthy, active circulating supply.

