17. Security Architecture

17.1 Slashing Conditions

Offense Detection Mechanism Penalty Additional Consequence
Double Proposal SafetyRules module 5% of stake burned Validator immediately deactivated
Double Vote VoteManager module 5% of stake burned Validator permanently slashed; cannot re-register
10 Consecutive ZK Benchmark Failures TitanNode tracking None (ejection only) Automatic removal from validator set
50+ Missed Block Proposals ValidatorRecord tracking None (jailing only) Validator jailed; must manually reactivate

17.2 Defense-in-Depth

The Sentinel Layer provides an independent, external detection path for equivocation. Even if consensus engine detection were compromised through a software bug, Sentinels would still observe and report violations, broadcasting SlashingEvidence to the network for penalty execution.

17.3 Long-Range Attack Resistance

HotStuff BFT's accountable safety property ensures that even if one-third of validators are malicious, honest validators can produce cryptographic quorum certificates proving which blocks were committed, preventing long-range fork attacks.

17.4 Write-Ahead Log Protection

All state mutations are written to an append-only log before being applied to the state database. On any unexpected termination, the WAL is replayed to restore the last consistent state, guaranteeing zero data loss from power failures, kernel panics, or unexpected process termination.

